# Comment Style Guide for SQL Queries

This guide defines preferred top-level comment block structures for SQL files in the `FAMCare-SQL-Toolkit` repository. Comment blocks should appear at the top of each `.sql` file to communicate purpose, logic, usage, and version history—especially for team members reviewing code outside of SSMS.

Comments should be enclosed in `/* ... */` and written in natural language. They serve as embedded documentation and historical record for each query.

---

## Exception Reports

```sql
/*
Report Name: [Title]
Category: Exception Reports

Purpose: Describe the exception being flagged (e.g. overlapping dates, missing forms, duplicated submissions).

Logic Summary:
- Identify key joins, filters, and logic used.
- Specify any logic thresholds (e.g. enrollment gaps > 90 days).

Usage Notes:
- Intended for internal review or staff remediation.

Changelog:
- YYYY-MM-DD: Initial creation.
- YYYY-MM-DD: Adjusted filter to exclude dismissed clients.
*/
```

## Program Management Reports

```sql
/*
Report Name: [Title]
Category: Program Management

Purpose: Summarize or segment data to support caseload tracking, grant monitoring, or service planning.

Key Metrics:
- Describe calculations, counts, or grouping logic.

Filters:
- Note any time-based or demographic constraints.

Changelog:
- YYYY-MM-DD: Initial version.
- YYYY-MM-DD: Added agency filter logic.
*/
```

## Audit Reports

```sql
/*
Report Name: [Title]
Category: Audit Reports

Purpose: Validate procedural compliance, user actions, or documentation completeness.

Audit Scope:
- List tracked actions (e.g. form submissions, report runs).
- Define timeframes or actors under review.

Changelog:
- YYYY-MM-DD: Initial version.
- YYYY-MM-DD: Expanded audit scope to include housing status forms.
*/
```

## Compiliance Reports

```sql
/*
Report Name: [Title]
Category: Compliance Reports

Purpose: Fulfill contractual, policy-based, or regulatory requirements through structured data export.

Compliance Scope:
- Define the regulation, grant, or external party receiving the report.
- Indicate required fields, formatting, and timing.

Usage Notes:
- Often part of recurring reporting obligations.
- May require versioned logic or formal approval before publishing.

Changelog:
- YYYY-MM-DD: Initial compliance report authored for [entity].
- YYYY-MM-DD: Added required eligibility field per updated policy.
*/
```

## External Data Sharing Reports

```sql
/*
Report Name: [Title]
Category: External Data Sharing Reports

Purpose: Provide structured data exports for approved non-contractual partners (e.g. research, coordination, voluntary sharing).

Sharing Context:
- Identify recipient agency or collaboration purpose.
- Clarify whether the request is recurring or ad hoc.

Usage Notes:
- Tailor filters and formatting to recipient needs.
- Ensure sharing complies with internal guidelines.

Changelog:
- YYYY-MM-DD: Initial version for [partner agency].
- YYYY-MM-DD: Renamed demographic fields for consistency with prior exports.
*/
```

## Extract Queries

```sql
/*
Report Name: [Title]
Category: Extract Queries

Purpose: Export structured data for use outside FAMCare or for analytical processing.

Output Description:
- List fields returned and their sources.
- Indicate whether data is filtered or raw.

Usage Notes:
- Intended for flat file export or dashboard input.

Changelog:
- YYYY-MM-DD: Initial query authored.
*/
```

## Maintenance Queries

```sql
/*
Query Title: [Title]
Category: Maintenance Queries

Purpose: Examine system-level objects or metadata to support troubleshooting, schema analysis, or performance review.

Scope:
- Review system tables, views, indexes, or procedures.
- Assess schema components without modifying data.

Usage Notes:
- These are read-only queries used by developers and database admins.
- Often paired with view creation or error diagnostics.

Changelog:
- YYYY-MM-DD: Initial maintenance query created.
- YYYY-MM-DD: Added filtering for sys.indexes by object type.
*/
```

## Maintentance Scripts (e.g., UPDATE, DELETE, INSERT)

```sql
/*
Script Title: [Title]
Category: Maintenance Scripts

Purpose: Apply data corrections or cleanup actions.

Reasoning:
- Summarize why rows need to be updated or removed.
- Reference related validation queries or reports.

Affected Rows:
- Describe targeted filtering logic.
- Estimate row count or scope, if known.

Execution Notes:
- Run in staging prior to any production deployment.

Changelog:
- YYYY-MM-DD: Script created for FY25 onboarding cleanup.
*/
```

## View Definitions

```sql
/*
View Name: [Title]
Category: View Definitions

Purpose: Encapsulate reusable logic for reporting or downstream joins.

Description:
- Summarize joins, calculated fields, and filters.
- State intended report dependencies.

Maintenance Notes:
- Changes here may affect multiple reports—document carefully.

Changelog:
- YYYY-MM-DD: Initial view definition authored.
*/
```
